WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.580
Telo Ride 1 now opens on its one class, Intervals to the Beat, and the class ships

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.673
with the app.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.689
Twenty minutes by GCN Training: seventeen efforts in thirty-three segments. The app

00:00:15.689 --> 00:00:20.773
reads it from its own code, so nothing is requested and nothing is cached.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.609
The plan is the one Ibiza Sunset Strip was built from, second for second. At five

00:00:28.609 --> 00:00:32.364
thirty the ride is in a recovery, at level thirteen.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:40.992
The class is checked each time it is read. If it breaks a rule it is not offered:

00:00:40.992 --> 00:00:44.352
the page says so, with reload, and no start button.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:53.444
The other classes are gone, with the client that fetched them, the backend's

00:00:53.444 --> 00:00:57.165
catalogue and seven courses. No other class has an address.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.035
The class fits a phone, a tablet and a desktop, as it did before.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:17.584
Seven specs came first, and all seven failed on the old class. Now one hundred and

00:01:17.584 --> 00:01:20.672
seventy-two specs and every unit test pass.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:30.825
Telo Ride 1, from the Telo family, is the focused edition of Telo Ride: one class,

00:01:30.825 --> 00:01:32.021
nothing else.

00:01:32.366 --> 00:01:37.318
It pairs with a smart bike at home over Bluetooth, plays the class video, or draws

00:01:37.318 --> 00:01:42.330
the Ibiza Sunset Strip course to music if the rider chooses it, and sets the bike's

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:45.831
resistance for every interval while the rider pedals.

00:01:46.176 --> 00:01:50.152
Connect the bike, take the class, see your number, and come back to beat it.
